NAME
    build.sh - build one staged m-boot GRUB image and external loader tree

SYNOPSIS
    ./build.sh --target x86_64-efi|arm64-efi|i386-pc --output DIR
               [--modules-dir DIR] [--grub-mkimage PATH]

DESCRIPTION
    Standalone Linux build: needs grub-mkimage with target-specific modules
    and tar. Uses the source boot/ files to produce an embedded memdisk, then
    stages the external loader/ directory beneath data/m/boot/loader/.
    Does not install, partition, format, or write to a block device.
    Fails rather than replacing an existing DIR/TARGET.

TARGETS
    x86_64-efi: DIR/x86_64-efi/esp/EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI
    arm64-efi:  DIR/arm64-efi/esp/EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI
    i386-pc:   DIR/i386-pc/bios/core.img (not directly bootable by copying)
    Every target includes data/m/boot/loader/ and stage-info.

OPTIONS
    --target        Required GRUB image format.
    --output        Required parent of new staged build directories.
    --modules-dir   Optional target-specific GRUB module directory; required
                    when cross-target modules aren't in a standard location.
    --grub-mkimage  Optional explicit GRUB image generator executable/path.
    --help          Print usage.

EXAMPLES
    ./build.sh --target x86_64-efi --output ./dist
    ./build.sh --target arm64-efi --output ./dist \
      --modules-dir /usr/lib/grub/arm64-efi

PERSISTENT ARM64 PACKAGE IN GIT
    The native Linux ARM64 GitHub Actions runner commits a compressed
    native build package into the repository on workflow-file updates:
        prebuilt/m-boot-arm64-efi.tar.xz
        prebuilt/m-boot-arm64-efi.tar.xz.sha256
    This tracked file is available through normal git pull and does not
    expire like GitHub Actions artifacts. To extract a full ARM64 stage
    and its modules into the combined QEMU stage directory:
        git pull --ff-only
        sha256sum -c prebuilt/m-boot-arm64-efi.tar.xz.sha256
        mkdir -p ./qemu-combined/stages
        tar -xJf prebuilt/m-boot-arm64-efi.tar.xz \
          -C ./qemu-combined/stages
    This provides both qemu-combined/stages/arm64-efi and
    qemu-combined/stages/grub-modules/arm64-efi. The archive includes
    arm64-build-info.txt with the original source revision and packages.
    On future workflow_dispatch runs, the GitHub Actions artifact is still
    produced, but the tracked archive is not silently replaced.

GITHUB ARM64 ARTIFACT
    For hosts without arm64-efi GRUB modules, the GitHub Actions workflow
    .github/workflows/build-grub-arm64.yml runs on ubuntu-24.04-arm.
    It runs this actual build.sh for arm64-efi and uploads the artifact
    m-boot-arm64-efi containing:
        arm64-efi/                  complete build stage (BOOTAA64.EFI)
        grub-modules/arm64-efi/    target GRUB modules
        arm64-build-info.txt      source revision and package versions
        BOOTAA64.EFI.sha256       checksum of the generated EFI image

    Download the artifact ZIP from the workflow run (Actions UI) and extract
    it into a stage parent directory. A GitHub CLI example is:
        gh run download RUN_ID -R massimilianonardi-ai/m-boot \
          -n m-boot-arm64-efi -D ./qemu-combined/stages

    To rebuild on an x86_64 Linux host using the extracted modules:
        ./build.sh --target arm64-efi --output ./other-stages \
          --modules-dir ./qemu-combined/stages/grub-modules/arm64-efi
    Do not put the newly built stage over an existing stage directory.
    GRUB modules must match the GRUB tools used to build the image.

NOTES
    The tool checks for required GRUB modules but does not prove that firmware
    will boot the resulting image. Test with GRUB/QEMU before deployment.
    The legacy target-build.sh remains untouched.

